From 661cea47c901d54e86998c92715b9bcde39fc3e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:54:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Map replica comment events by comment_uid; record
 stored len; no trailing space in wake note

A replica could not map the dispatcher's CI wake note ("Woken: ... (PR url). ") to its commented
event, so it counted as a new PR publication and held the card active_pr for 10 min
(t_eeeeee000000001f, example incident).

Five whys: held active_pr -> wake note newer than the owner's park looked like an own-run PR comment
-> _event_row_id could not map the event to its replica row (payload comment_id is the home id;
the (created_at, author, len) triple failed) -> add_comment stored body.strip() but recorded
len(body), and the note had a trailing space -> the mapping ignored comment_uid, which both sides carry.

- kanban_db_dispatch_pr_state: _comment_rows reads uid when present; _event_row_id maps by the
  payload comment_uid to the unique local row first. Zero or several matches fall back to the old
  triple / comment_id logic, so it never fails open.
- kanban_db_comment_ids.add_comment: record len(body.strip()), the stored length.
- kanban_external_watch._finished_note: join parts, no trailing space.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_pr_replica_comment_uid.py (RED on main: 5 failed; GREEN with
the change), plus 49 files importing the changed modules: 1118 passed.

Hermes-Card: t_eeeeee000000002c
